{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480319-i-need-aclaration-about-tools","id":1480319,"title":"I need aclaration about tools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-06T16:22:27-07:00","id":1480319,"title":"I need aclaration about tools","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> Most exactly, I want aclaration about Path and Order tools: What defines them and how are they use?<br /> <br /> My problem is sometimes I feel that magical tools need to be &quot;prepared&quot;, like, a Moros can't take <i>any</i> spent bullet and gain a Yantra from it to make plants grow, no?<br /> <br /> In other moments it seems that anything can be a Yantra at anytime, something I don't have a immediate problem, but I want to be clarified about this.<br /> <br /> In general I never think to much about this, but I read Signs of Sorcery and the perfected material. &quot;If the perfected material is use as a <b>Path Tool</b> it gives the Repeat 9s quality&quot;, what is the difference about something use as a Path Tool, something use as a Order Tool and any of the other Yantras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T17:02:02-07:00","id":1480325,"title":"","content":"Path Tools are the categories defined on page 121 of the corebook, plus any Artifacts whose highest Arcanum belongs to the Path. They're used as instruments that tend to symbolize the process the spell is performing.<br /> <br /> Order Tools are as defined in their orders' writeups, as well as any additional methods provided by Order Merits. Their symbolism likewise tends to focus their utility in a particular direction depending on the order.<br /> <br /> The limitation on a thing's utility as a Yantra is that the mage in question has to recognize a meaningful semiotic value in it; there's an entire category of Yantra defined by being consumed with their use, and bonuses above +1 tend to require drawbacks or difficulty in their engagement.<br /> <br /> If you're using something as a Path Tool, you're using it as a Coin, Cup, Mirror, Rod, or Weapon, and it's primarily made of one of the corresponding materials in the sidebar, which is where the perfected materials factor in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T10:08:25-07:00","id":1480372,"title":"","content":"The only tools that seem to have any explicit need for preparation are dedicated tools to reduce Paradox. Otherwise it's a matter of the process of coming to acquire them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T10:26:53-07:00","id":1481090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480319-i-need-aclaration-about-tools#post1480319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello!<br /> ...<br /> <br /> My problem is sometimes I feel that magical tools need to be &quot;prepared&quot;, like, a Moros can't take <i>any</i> spent bullet and gain a Yantra from it to make plants grow, no?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> In general I never think to much about this, but I read Signs of Sorcery and the perfected material. &quot;If the perfected material is use as a <b>Path Tool</b> it gives the Repeat 9s quality&quot;, what is the difference about something use as a Path Tool, something use as a Order Tool and any of the other Yantras?</div> </div> </div> </div>A yantra needs to be a symbol that fits the spell being cast. Thus, a random spent bullet casing is unlikely to help as a yantra for casting a life spell for regrowth. A spent bullet casing from the shot that liberated a city from the brutal reign of a crime boss, triggering a renewal, on the other hand? Yeah, that's a solid yantra. Depending how you mean &quot;prepared&quot;, that might qualify.<br /> <br /> The sole (to my knowledge) exception to the normal rule that a yantra must fit the symbolism of the spell being cast is the dedicated magical tool. (Personally, I don't think removing that exception to the symbolism requirement causes any problems, but it <i>is</i> a house rule.)<br /> <br /> Mechanically, you have a limited number of Yantras that you can apply to a spell casting. This might be better written as &quot;number of yantra applications&quot; because a single object can be used in a number of different ways. Each way that you use a thing counts against your limit. <br /> <br /> If you have a dedicated wand of the proper material for your path you could use it as a wand (path tool), or as a dedicated magical tool, both, or neither. If you use it twice, it counts against your totals twice and you'd get benefit for both ways in which it applies. In that example, you could get the benefit of the dedicated magic tool (-2 to paradox die pools) and as a path tool (generally a simple +1 yantra bonus)<br /> <br /> (Depending how you read the effect of a dedicated magical tool, you might read it as getting both for a single application, making this a poor example but it's a common one, so I tossed it in.)<br /> <br /> If a time, place, or object is symbolically important in multiple ways, you could use it for those different ways. An ivory wand carved from the tusk of an elephant that the subject saved, for example, could be a remarkably good yantra when you are trying to restore a subject's magically removed memories, it might be both a focusing tool as well as a symbolic of durable legacy and memory and, of course, the symbolism of an elephant's memory.<br /> <br /> There's room for argument that a stacked meaning like that should simply be a single, higher rated yantra. Really, the difference is up to how the ST runs things.<br /> <br /> The rules for yantras are broadly worded, so the even how well the symbols need to fit the spell is up to the storyteller and your gaming crew. I prefer a fairly narrow interpretation because the idea of using nonsense seems silly to me.<br /> <br /> Yantra rules are arbitrary so a group can make them support the themes of magic that they like. That leaves things somewhat vulnerable to argumentation but does allow a group to run things to taste. Some may prefer a very strict analysis of what's allowed while another group permits things even vaguely symbolic to the desired effect to count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T02:47:45-07:00","id":1481167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480319-i-need-aclaration-about-tools?p=1481090#post1481090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A yantra needs to be a symbol that fits the spell being cast. Thus, a random spent bullet casing is unlikely to help as a yantra for casting a life spell for regrowth. A spent bullet casing from the shot that liberated a city from the brutal reign of a crime boss, triggering a renewal, on the other hand? Yeah, that's a solid yantra. Depending how you mean &amp;quot;prepared&amp;quot;, that might qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also needs to fit a Yantra category the character has access to. I don't see how you'd use a spent bullet casing as a Yantra, regardless of its history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T03:30:59-07:00","id":1481169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480319-i-need-aclaration-about-tools?p=1481167#post1481167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also needs to fit a Yantra category the character has access to. I don't see how you'd use a spent bullet casing as a Yantra, regardless of its history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> had spent bullets as a type of Coin-type Path Tool Yantra for Moros, via Ars Nova. Though we\u2019ll have to see that book again to be certain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T06:04:05-07:00","id":1481173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480319-i-need-aclaration-about-tools?p=1481169#post1481169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> had spent bullets as a type of Coin-type Path Tool Yantra for Moros, via Ars Nova. Though we\u2019ll have to see that book again to be certain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly right.<br /> <br /> On the matter of preparation, that same chart lists &quot;improvised weapon&quot; in the Moros category for Weapon tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T06:16:00-07:00","id":1481174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480319-i-need-aclaration-about-tools?p=1481169#post1481169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> had spent bullets as a type of Coin-type Path Tool Yantra for Moros, via Ars Nova. Though we\u2019ll have to see that book again to be certain.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. Spent bullets are considered Coins for Moros. But that means it's a Path Tool, so the history of the bullet (other than the fact it has been fired at some point) still doesn't matter. The reason it can be used as a Path Tool is because of how the symbolism of the bullet (bringer of death, propelled by modern alchemy) relates to the Path of Moros (necromancers and alchemists). And if used as a Coin, it can naturally only grant bonuses according to its role as a Coin.<br /> <br /> The history of objects can matter for whether they qualify as Path Tools (the Ars Nova Coins for Mastigos are all about that, and objects that have been buried can replace the material aspect for other Moros Path Tools), but when used as Yantras they're limited to the symbolism of the type of Path Tool rather than anything about the individual objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T07:17:58-07:00","id":1481175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480319-i-need-aclaration-about-tools?p=1481174#post1481174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right. Spent bullets are considered Coins for Moros. But that means it's a Path Tool, so the history of the bullet (other than the fact it has been fired at some point) still doesn't matter. The reason it can be used as a Path Tool is because of how the symbolism of the bullet (bringer of death, propelled by modern alchemy) relates to the Path of Moros (necromancers and alchemists). And if used as a Coin, it can naturally only grant bonuses according to its role as a Coin.<br /> <br /> The history of objects can matter for whether they qualify as Path Tools (the Ars Nova Coins for Mastigos are all about that, and objects that have been buried can replace the material aspect for other Moros Path Tools), but when used as Yantras they're limited to the symbolism of the type of Path Tool rather than anything about the individual objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I see.<br /> <br /> So for the initial example of pcasting healing spells with it\u2026 uh\u2026 Coins symbolize the material world, and the Moros could very much have a materialistic understanding of biochemical functions, so there\u2019s that for healing magic I guess? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T08:59:28-07:00","id":1481178,"title":"","content":"Coins symbolize repair. Cups symbolize healing.<br /> <br /> I'd say there are forms of both of those things that would differ enough to mean they're not completely interchangeable tools within those functions, but that either would suffice for the function of fixing a damaged body.<br /> <br /> For the idea of making plants grow... I could see that as a function of the symbolism of construction, although a rod might be a closer fit.<br /> <br /> In any case, the important thing is to understand that the tool in and of itself isn't what is being applied, it's the principles that it can be abstracted into. Arguably the Ars Nova consists of adding a few more layers to the abstraction, but it still ends up in the same place. That's what allows engagement with it to function as a reference in the forming of an imago.<br /> <br /> This often makes me think about the description of the Alethiometer in Northern Lights; how the symbols inscribed on it are few, but each one has layers of meaning so that between them they can be used to form almost any inquiry. The character of Lyra possesses a knack for knowing how to use the thing to dig into those layers and understand which one is being used when they symbol is pointed back to her, where most people require a lot of practice and some amount of consultation with books to know the full depth of each symbol's meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}